# 🛒 Global Superstore — Sales & Profit Dashboard in Excel

> An end-to-end Excel analytics project: data cleaning, transformation, business Q&A, and an interactive dashboard — built on the Global Superstore dataset.

![Dashboard Preview](Dashboard.png)

---

## 📌 Project Overview

Superstores operate across vast geographies and product lines. To stay competitive, businesses need a clear, real-time view of their key performance indicators. This project takes raw transactional data and turns it into a decision-ready Excel dashboard — answering six critical business questions along the way.

**Dataset:** Global Superstore Sales (Kaggle)  
**Tool:** Microsoft Excel  
**Skills demonstrated:** Data cleaning · VLOOKUP · Pivot Tables · Dashboard design · Business insight generation

---

## 🗂️ Dataset Structure

The workbook contains three sheets that were combined into a single analysis-ready table:

| Sheet | Description |
|---|---|
| Orders | Transaction-level sales data across regions, categories, and segments |
| People | Regional manager mapping |
| Returned Items | Records of returned orders |

The `People` and `Returned Items` sheets were merged into `Orders` using **VLOOKUP**.

---

## 🧹 Data Cleaning Steps

### Step 1 — Merge sheets
Joined `People` and `Returned Items` into the main Orders table via VLOOKUP on the Order ID key.

### Step 2 — Handle duplicates & nulls
- **Duplicates:** Checked via *Data → Remove Duplicates* — none found.
- **Null values:** Checked via *Home → Find & Select → Go To Special* — none found.
- **Postal Code** column dropped: only a fraction of rows had valid codes; not useful for analysis.

### Step 3 — Feature engineering
New columns created to enable time-series and profitability analysis:

| New Column | Derived From | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `Year` | Order Date | Year-over-year trend analysis |
| `Month` | Order Date | Monthly seasonality |
| `Month_name` | Order Date | Human-readable labels in charts |
| `LOSS` | Profit (negatives) | Isolate loss-making transactions |

**Removed:** `Postal Code`, `Row Number`

---

## ❓ Business Questions Answered

| # | Question |
|---|---|
| Q1 | Which customer segment is the top revenue driver? |
| Q2 | How does sales profit vary by category over the years? |
| Q3 | Which region has the highest order count — and where should we focus growth? |
| Q4 | How does performance break down by country? |
| Q5 | What are the top 10 best-selling products? |
| Q6 | What is the total profit, total loss, and net profit of the superstore? |

---

## 📊 Dashboard

The interactive dashboard surfaces all six business questions in a single view, with slicers for **Year**, **Segment**, and **Category**.

![Dashboard](Dashboard.png)

